# CB File Hub - build-time configuration
#
# Copy to `.env` in this same folder and fill in the values you have. `.env` is
# git-ignored; this example file is not, so never put real values here.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Two consumers read it:
#   * scripts/build.sh  - loads this file, then passes every non-empty value as
#                         --dart-define (real environment variables win over it)
#   * flutter directly  - flutter run -d windows --dart-define-from-file=../.env
#                         (run from cb_file_manager/, hence the ../)
#
# Everything here is optional. A provider whose ids are missing is simply shown
# as unavailable in Backup & Sync; the build still succeeds.
#
# See docs/features/08-cloud-backup-sync.md for how to register the clients.

# --- Google Drive ------------------------------------------------------------
# "Desktop app" OAuth client - Windows, macOS and Linux.
# Both are required on desktop. The secret is not confidential (it ships inside
# the binary; PKCE is the real protection), but a Desktop app client rejects the
# token exchange with "client_secret is missing" when it is left out.
GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# "Web application" OAuth client of the SAME project - required on Android.
# Credential Manager authenticates against this one. The Android client
# (package name + SHA-1) is matched by signature and never appears here.
GOOGLE_DRIVE_SERVER_CLIENT_ID=

# --- Dropbox -----------------------------------------------------------------
# App key of a scoped app. Desktop only.
# Register http://127.0.0.1:53682, :53683 and :53684 as redirect URIs.
DROPBOX_APP_KEY=

# --- OneDrive ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Application (client) id of an Entra ID registration with a
# "Mobile and desktop applications" platform and redirect http://127.0.0.1.
ONEDRIVE_CLIENT_ID=
